All nine images are visible in the stated order. This review covers the local ensemble renders only; live placement and walking access remain unverified.

- **Woodyard — acceptable for deployment visual gate.** The timber frame, roof, log storage, and workbench read clearly as a woodyard. The hanging sign obscures part of the wall panel from the front, but the interior angle shows that the panel remains exposed behind it; there is no clear burial defect. The bench surface is accessible-looking, with timber stored beneath and alongside it. The “aerial” image looks upward at the roof underside, so it does not verify exterior roof closure. No definite roof opening or floating structural support is visible.

- **Bakery — must fix roof closure and verify review targeting.** The aerial view shows a substantial uncovered strip between the two roof masses, above what appears to be a continuous enclosed, tiled workspace. Close this opening or establish that it is an intentional open courtyard with appropriately terminated enclosure. The front view communicates baking through the oven and bread table, with a clear-looking entrance. However, the supplied bakery interior shows a forge hearth, anvil, and quench barrel. This may be an adjoining trade bay, but it does not verify the bakery’s interior workspace; the relationship needs a correctly framed view before the whole assembly can pass.

- **Forge — must fix the detached sign assembly.** In the aerial view, the hanging sign, bracket, and long horizontal backing member stand apart from the chimney and work area, with no visible supporting wall or post. Connect that assembly to its intended support or correct its placement. The forge itself reads clearly through the hearth, chimney, anvil, and water barrel; the work area looks approachable. The protected art and its backing are judged as part of the assembly, with no art replacement requested. The close hearth view shows daylight between the arch crown and the structure above; whether that is an intended throat opening or an enclosure defect remains unverified.

**Gate result:** woodyard passes visually; bakery and forge require the specific corrections or verification above. No Bill approval is implied.
